---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Praneeth Paikray, a Solutions Architect working on production AI systems, agent evaluation, and technical education.">
  <header class="page-intro container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Engineer, explainer, persistent evaluator.</h1>
  </header>

  <section class="about-grid container">
    <div class="portrait" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="initials">PP</div>
      <p>Bengaluru<br />India</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p class="lede">I’m Praneeth Paikray, a Solutions Architect focused on making ambitious AI ideas work inside real organizations.</p>
      <p>Over the last nine years, I have worked across enterprise IT, financial services, staffing, and data platforms. The recurring pattern is simple: the model is rarely the whole system. The difficult and interesting work sits around it, in data, tools, evaluation, interfaces, operations, and the judgment to know what should be automated.</p>
      <p>At Databricks, I work with teams building production GenAI and agent systems. Outside customer work, I build open-source experiments, design technical workshops, and write about what I learn. My recent work spans agent evaluation harnesses, autonomous AI engineering, document intelligence, real-time agents, and multilingual systems.</p>

      <h2>What I care about</h2>
      <div class="values">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Measured, not asserted</h3>
          <p>A fluent demo is a starting point. Claims should survive traces, held-out tests, model swaps, and the boring edge cases.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Useful technical depth</h3>
          <p>I like explanations that preserve the tradeoffs and implementation detail without turning jargon into a personality.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Reusable work</h3>
          <p>A good workshop or demo should leave behind an asset that another engineer can understand, adapt, and run.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>Find my code on <a href="https://github.com/Praneeth16">GitHub</a>, shorter updates on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/praneeth-paikray/">LinkedIn</a>, earlier essays on <a href="https://medium.com/@paikraypraneeth">Medium</a>, and models or datasets on <a href="https://huggingface.co/Praneeth">Hugging Face</a>.</p>
      <p>For workshops, speaking, or a thoughtful technical conversation, connect with me on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/praneeth-paikray/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(250px, 0.42fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
    padding-bottom: 7rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .portrait {
    position: sticky;
    top: 2rem;
    min-height: 420px;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--paper-soft);
    background: var(--moss);
    box-shadow: 10px 10px 0 var(--sun);
  }

  .initials {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(8rem, 16vw, 13rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.1em;
    line-height: 0.8;
  }

  .portrait p {
    position: absolute;
    right: 1.2rem;
    bottom: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    text-align: right;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .about-copy {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .lede {
    margin-top: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.22;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 4rem 0 1.4rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 520;
  }

  .values {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .values article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 42px 1fr;
    gap: 0 1rem;
    padding: 1.3rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .values span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .values h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 520;
  }

  .values p {
    grid-column: 2;
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .portrait {
      position: relative;
      min-height: 260px;
      top: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
